plugin-hostd-protocol (0.5.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Built against plugin-db >= 0.4.4 and below 0.5 and omx-dsp >= 0.32.1 and
    below 0.33, the 3.18.0 pass's newest of each, with their ceilings (D30).
  * CI renders against what the channel serves every day, the render check
    alone, and names the served contract packages when it fails (#27, #32).
  * The fuzz seed corpus is held to its generator on every pull request, and
    the generator writes the same corpus in every locale (LC_ALL=C); the
    corpus and both golden transcripts are written again over it (#33, #34).
  * The default CLAP search path holds the folders distributions install
    plugins in, /usr/local/lib/clap, /usr/lib64/clap and /usr/local/lib64/clap,
    after clap/entry.h's: a fresh plugin-hostd learns a first-use pin there
    (plugin-hostd#82, #36).

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100

